<% prefix = assigns[:domain_prefix] || "<prefix>" %>## Command reference

MCP tool first; the `arb` CLI is the fallback for when MCP isn't connected, or
for the handful of verbs with no MCP equivalent yet (marked **—**). If you are
telling the *operator* to do something, give them the `arb` command, never
MCP tool-call syntax — they only have a terminal.

| Command | MCP tool | What it does |
|---------|----------|--------------|
| `arb doctor` | — | Health check — server reachable, workspace exists |
| `arb prime` | — | Session-start briefing + standing orders |
| `arb ticket list` | `ticket_list` | List tickets |
| `arb ticket ready` | `ticket_ready` | Tickets with all dependencies closed — ready to work |
| `arb ticket show <id>` | `ticket_show` | Detail on a single ticket |
| `arb ticket create <title>` | `ticket_create` | Create a ticket (`--priority`, `--difficulty`, `--type`) |
| `arb ticket update <id>` | `ticket_update` | Update a ticket's fields |
| `arb ticket close <id>` | `ticket_close` | Close a ticket |
| `arb ticket reopen <id>` | `ticket_reopen` | Reopen a closed ticket |
| `arb ticket claim <ref>` | `tracker_claim` | Claim an upstream tracker issue as a local ticket |
| `arb ticket sync` | `tracker_sync` | Reconcile tickets against the tracker |
| `arb dep add <from> <type> <to>` | `dep_add` | Add a dependency (e.g. `arb dep add <%= prefix %>-1 blocks <%= prefix %>-2`) |
| `arb dep remove <from> <to>` | `dep_remove` | Remove a dependency |
<%= if assigns[:can_dispatch] do %>| `arb ticket dispatch <id> [<repo>] --provider claude` | `worker_dispatch` | Dispatch a ticket to a live worker (**costs API credits**) |
<% end %>| `arb worker list` | `worker_list` | List active workers |
| `arb worker show <task-id>` | `worker_show` | Worker detail and output |
| `arb worker stop <task-id>` | `worker_stop` | Stop a running worker |
| `arb worker resume <task-id>` | `worker_resume` | Reattach a fresh session to a preserved worktree |
| `arb worker review <task-id>` | `worker_review` | Review a PR/MR tracker-side |
| `arb attention` | `coordinator_inbox` | Unread events needing the coordinator |
| `arb message inbox <task-id>` | `inbox_check` | Read/clear a ticket's mailbox |
| `arb message send <recipient> <body>` | `message_send` | Leave a message in a ticket's mailbox |
| `arb config get / set / unset <key>` | `workspace_config_get` / `_set` / `_unset` | Read or deep-merge-update workspace config (never raw API PATCH) |
| `arb quota` | `quota_get` | Current provider rate-limit/quota state |
| `arb where` | `workspace_show` | Which workspace is active |

All CLI commands accept `--json` for machine-readable output. Use
`-w, --workspace <name>` (or `ARB_WORKSPACE`) to target a specific workspace.
